neatvnc is a VNC server library implementing the RFB protocol. It
supports raw, ZRLE, and Tight encodings, TLS and VeNCrypt auth,
websocket transport, and optional H.264 encoding. It is used by wayvnc.

This package installs the shared library, headers, and pkg-config file
required to build wayvnc.

Requirements (all part of the Slackware base system):
  - meson
  - ninja
  - pixman
  - zlib
  - libdrm
  - gnutls (TLS)
  - nettle (crypto and websocket support)
  - libjpeg-turbo (JPEG)
  - gbm (dmabuf)

Optional:
  - ffmpeg enables H.264 encoding via libavcodec/libavfilter.

SBo dependencies:
  - aml
